-- Examples (the results below are what this file gives; each matches a real figure):
--   1. Class scores equal the school's real test mean:
--        SELECT ROUND(AVG(score), 1), ROUND(STDDEV_POP(score), 1)
--        FROM LITERACY WHERE class_ID = 2 AND attempt_no = 1;
--      -> 66.4 and 12.9. Riverside School's real 2025-26 Grade 9 English Language Arts test:
--         mean 66.4, standard deviation 13.0.
--   2. Schools with the lowest average literacy (Question 2, with the LOCALITY join fixed and
--      the lowest first):
--        SELECT s.school_name, ROUND(AVG(l.score), 1) AS score
--        FROM LITERACY l JOIN CLASS c ON c.class_ID = l.class_ID
--        JOIN SCHOOL s ON s.school_ID = c.school_ID
--        JOIN LOCALITY lo ON lo.locality_ID = s.locality_id
--        WHERE lo.country_ID = 1 AND l.attempt_no = 1
--        GROUP BY s.school_name ORDER BY score LIMIT 3;
--      -> Mistassiniy School 47.3, Ernest Morrow School 48.9, Patrick Airlie School 50.6.
--         Real test means: 47.4, 48.9 and 50.6. The highest is Webber Academy, 85.9 (real 85.9).
--   3. Absence rate (Calgary public schools, academic year 2025):
--        SELECT ROUND(100 * AVG(a.attendance = 'absent'), 1)
--        FROM ATTENDANCE a JOIN SESSION se ON se.session_ID = a.session_ID
--        JOIN CLASS c ON c.class_ID = se.class_ID JOIN SCHOOL s ON s.school_ID = c.school_ID
--        JOIN LOCALITY lo ON lo.locality_ID = s.locality_id
--        WHERE s.ownership_type = 'Public' AND lo.locality_name LIKE 'AB-CAL-%'
--          AND c.academic_year = 2025 AND c.grade_level IN (8, 9);
--      -> 11.9. Calgary Board of Education 2024-25, Grades 7-9: 11.7.
--         With grade_level IN (5, 6): 8.2. Calgary Board of Education, Grades 4-6: 8.9.
--   4. Absence reasons (the same joins and WHERE as example 3):
--        SELECT ROUND(100 * SUM(a.absence_reason IS NULL) / COUNT(*), 1),
--               ROUND(100 * SUM(a.absence_reason = 'Illness') / COUNT(*), 1)
--        ... AND a.attendance = 'absent';
--      -> 41.9% without guardian contact and 30.6% illness. Calgary Board of Education,
--         Grades 7-9: 36% and 33%.
--   5. Schools where many students missed the real test also miss more classes: Ernest Morrow
--      School has the most absences (25.7% of attendance rows; 20% of its students missed the
--      real Grade 9 English test). Webber Academy is among the lowest (4.9%; nobody missed the
--      test).
--   6. The October 2025 teachers' strike: sessions between 2025-10-06 and 2025-10-28 by
--      SCHOOL.ownership_type -> Public 0, Catholic 0, Charter 14, Private 14 (charter and
--      private schools stayed open).
--   7. Extreme cold days: WHERE a.absence_reason = 'Extreme cold weather' finds real cold days,
--      for example 2025-12-11 in Fort McMurray (high of -23.4 C). On its 7 cold session days
--      Fort McMurray (locality 14) has 8.2% absence, against 6.3% on the other 84 days.
--   8. Boys and girls (Question 3): attendance in AB-CAL-NE (locality 3) is 86.7% for boys and
--      90.2% for girls; over all localities, 89.9% and 91.0%. Boys skip more often, as in the
--      Statistics Canada survey (boys skip 1.16 times as many days as girls).
--   9. Funding (Question 4): SUM(FUNDING.amount) by school -> Peter Lougheed School 356409 CAD,
--      Westwood Community High School 353287 CAD, Prince of Peace School 338325 CAD: each
--      school's enrolment share of the real grants paid to its school authority.
--  10. Literacy rate of a country (Question 1): CANADA, statistics_year 2022 -> 80.7.
--  11. The team's queries in "Project Queries.sql" still work: each INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE
--      changes 1 row, Sobia (teacher_ID 2) has 4 classes, 140 students were absent on
--      2025-09-02 (Amy Black: 'Medical appointment'), and 3 LITERACY rows of class 2 have
--      score <= 50.

